  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "FishPix",
  "description": "FishPix is a database of 35,000 photographs of fishes. FishPix consists primarily of photographs of Japanese fishes but also includes those taken in the tropical western Pacific, the Indian Ocean, the Caribbean Sea, and other parts of the world. Although ichthyologists have provided many photographs, the majority has been sent from amateur SCUBA divers. The assistance of the diving community is gratefully acknowledged.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: The Fish Divisions of the Kanagawa Prefectural Museum of Natural History, Odawara, and the National Science Museum, Tokyo, joined forces in 1998 to build this database.",
